<description>
Recolor each solid rectangle into nested alternating interior layers.

Input structure
- The input has one empty background color and one foreground color.
- Under the correct background choice, the foreground forms one or more
  4-connected filled axis-aligned rectangles.

Rule
- Keep each rectangle's outer border in the original foreground color.
- Recolor pixels at odd positive distance from the rectangle edge red.
- Recolor pixels at even positive distance from the rectangle edge green.

Key insight
- The new colors depend only on each pixel's rectangular layer depth; the
  rectangles themselves do not move or resize.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "4-connected filled foreground rectangles on an empty background",
  "transform": "keep each rectangle's outer border unchanged; recolor each positive-depth rectangular layer red for odd depth and green for even depth"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 11-17 rows x 11-17 cols
  colors:
    input: exactly 2 colors -- bg=0(black) and fg=1(blue)
    output: bg unchanged; rect border stays fg; interior layers recolored to red(2) and green(3)
  rectangles:
    count: 2-3 solid filled axis-aligned rectangles of color fg
    dimensions: each at least 3x3; individual side 3-11; at least one rect with min(h,w) >= 5 [observed]
    placement: non-overlapping, 4-connected separated (min 1 bg cell gap between any two)
    may touch grid edges [observed]
    coverage: ~40-55% of grid area [observed]
  transform:
    for each rectangle, compute depth = min distance to rectangle border
    depth 0 (border) -> keep fg (blue=1)
    depth odd (1,3,...) -> red (2)
